Only 1 failed because `-t incomplete` matches one test (the other test name has "incomplete"? Backups test "offers the pre-operation backup after a failed restore" doesn't include incomplete; so skipped). Fine. Implement.

Create `recovery.ts` and `JobRecovery.svelte`.

`recovery.ts`:
```ts
export function recoveryDatabaseName(database: string, now = new Date()): string {
  const stamp = now.toISOString().replace(/[-:T]/g,'').slice(0,14);
  const suffix = `_recovery_${stamp}`;
  const maxBase = 63 - suffix.length;
  const base = database.slice(0, Math.max(1, maxBase));
  return `${base}${suffix}`;
}
```
If base ends with invalid? It's truncated original valid identifier; still valid. Good.

`JobRecovery.svelte`:
Props `{ service, job, onrecovered }`.
- `const recoveryEligible = $derived((job.status === 'failed' || job.status === 'canceled') && Boolean(job.backup_id) && (job.kind === 'restore' || job.kind === 'import'));`
- State open, busy, error.
- `const targetName = $derived(recoveryDatabaseName(job.database));`
- confirm:
```ts
const backupID = job.backup_id;
if (!backupID || busy) return;
busy = true; error=null;
try { const next = await dbApi.restoreServiceBackup(service.id, backupID, { target: targetName, overwrite:false, confirm: job.database, pre_restore_backup:false }); open=false; onrecovered(next); }
catch { error=describeError(caught); } finally { busy=false; }
```
- Markup:
```svelte
{#if recoveryEligible}
  <div class="recovery" role="alert">
    <p><strong>Restore incomplete.</strong> {job.database} may be partially modified.</p>
    <Button size="sm" variant="secondary" onclick={()=>{error=null;open=true}}>Restore pre-operation backup</Button>
  </div>
  <ConfirmDialog open={open} title={`Restore pre-operation backup for ${job.database}?`} description={`Restores the pre-operation backup into ${targetName}. The incomplete target is not overwritten.`} confirmLabel="Restore backup" busy={busy} requireText={job.database} onconfirm={confirm} oncancel={()=>{if(!busy) open=false}}>
    {#snippet details()}{#if error}<p role=alert>...</p>{/if}{/snippet}
  </ConfirmDialog>
{/if}
```
- The test `findByText(/restore incomplete/i)` sees `<strong>Restore incomplete.</strong>`; exact regex matches. Good.
- Button accessible name "Restore pre-operation backup". Good.
- Dialog requireText label `Type "app" to confirm` (curly in actual). Good.
- Confirm button label "Restore backup" unique within dialog.
- On success, parent `watchJob` will show toast based on status succeeded. Good.

Integrate in DatabaseTab and BackupsTab after job message:
```svelte
<JobRecovery {service} {job} onrecovered={watchJob} />
```
Import component.

Need ensure `JobRecovery` only shows for restore/import, not backup failed. Good.

