Good.

Need tests:
1. Deactivate warning inventory unavailable: set backupsError; click deactivate; confirm disabled and text unavailable.
2. Cross-tab active job: route test as described.
3. Maybe activeJob callback test in DatabaseTab.

Add route test mock createServiceBackup. Current ServiceDetail.test databaseApi mock factory has listServiceDatabases/listUsers/listBackups only. Add createServiceBackup: vi.fn(), getDatabaseJob maybe. Add `vi.mocked(db.createServiceBackup).mockResolvedValue(RUNNING_JOB)` in test.

Test:
```ts
it('warns about a running job after switching tabs', async () => {
 const running = {...};
 vi.mocked(db.createServiceBackup).mockResolvedValue(running);
 render mysql;
 await findByRole heading;
 await fireEvent.click(await screen.findByRole('button',{name:/back up app/i}));
 await waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByRole('status',{name:'Database job'})).toBeTruthy());
 await fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('tab',{name:'Users'}));
 await fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button',{name:'Deactivate'}));
 const dialog = await screen.findByRole('dialog');
 expect(within(dialog).getByText(/backup on app/i)).toBeTruthy();
});
```
- DatabaseTab has Back up app button for app. `MYSQL_DATABASES` app linked to blog; backup doesn't require stop. Good.
- `createServiceBackup` mock. Need import type DatabaseJob? Test already imports DatabaseBackup/User/Database. Add DatabaseJob or inline cast. Use `as DatabaseJob` import.
- After click Users tab, DatabaseTab unmounts; onDestroy stopJobPolling no longer clears activeJob. Good.
- Deactivate dialog opens. Confirm disabled? Inventory available, no. It will show running backup jobs 0 plus backup on app. Text `plus backup on app`; regex /backup on app/i.
- The route's transient poll may call load every 1.5s; no issue.

Test inventory unavailable:
- `vi.mocked(db.listServiceBackups).mockRejectedValue(new Error('backup index unavailable'));`
- render; wait heading; click Deactivate; dialog; expect text /backup inventory failed to load/i; confirm disabled.
- Existing test "keeps one failed inventory call..." uses same error but doesn't deactivate. Add.

Let's add tests.

